course: dictionary
lesson: 5075
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for instrument. It can be a thing used to make music, or a tool used for measuring or careful work. Context, the words around it, tells you which one the writer means.
explain: «Before an orchestra plays, the players tune up, and everyone matches the note A on their instruments.» Orchestra, players, tune and note all belong to music, so instruments here are things that make music. Always ask: what does this word mean in this sentence, and does my meaning fit the other words?
explain: Other sentences point to the second meaning. A thermometer and a ruler are instruments because they measure, and a doctor's tools are instruments because they do careful work. «The recorder is a real instrument» tells you that it is a musical instrument, because composers wrote music for it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context shows you which meaning is right.
fact: An «instrument» is a thing used to make music, like a piano, guitar, violin, flute or drum.
fact: An «instrument» is also a tool for measuring or doing careful work, like a ruler, thermometer or a doctor's tools.
fact: Phrases help too: «musical instrument», «play an instrument», «measuring instrument» and «string instrument».
exercise: «Before an orchestra plays, the players tune up, and everyone matches the note A on their instruments.» What are instruments in this sentence? | *Things used to make music | Kinds of weather | Tools for measuring | Parts of a house
exercise: Which of these is a musical instrument? | scales | *violin | ruler | thermometer
exercise: «Every corner of the world built its own instruments from what was at hand: gourds, termite-hollowed branches, bamboo, old oil drums.» Find and copy one material that was used to make instruments. | world | corner | stories | *bamboo
test:
«The doctor checked my heart with her instruments.» What does instrument mean here? | A kind of cloud | A thing for playing a tune | *A tool for careful work | A type of bread
test:
«Learning an instrument is like building a wall brick by brick: a little practice every day works better than one long session a week.» What does this comparison tell you? | *Small steps every day add up, like bricks in a wall | Bricks are musical instruments | Walls can play music | Practice should be done only once a week
exam:
Lena reads «The scientist checked the temperature with a thermometer, a measuring instrument.» What does measuring instrument mean? | A cake recipe | *A tool for measuring | A kind of song | A dance step
